> My impression is that lower level spells cost less energy
> points and also cost less nutrition points.  

True, but they also exercise spellcasting less, and to the same ratio.
Net, you get the same amount of exercise per spell point and per
nutrition; all three are proportional to the spell's level.

There is one difference which may be advantageous or not depending on
your strategy: lower level spells take more turns to gain that exercise
and lose those points and nutrition. So casting lower level spells
actually makes you _more_ hungry; not because the casting itself costs
more nutrition, but because you also lose it through simply taking
turns.

